            it touched; putting a head on the wire (`sendLane`) is the one unnoted move. Why: a write per send doubled
            batches for no new bytes. Reverse: per-move saves.
        comment     2026-11-16T10:03:02Z
            [decided: agent builder 2026-11-16] A Recapturing head's lane record carries retryCount + 1 while memory
            keeps the invoked count, and a refused batch goes again after 5 s whatever captureMs is. Why: a refused
            capture needs no undo, and captureMs 0 never loops on a refusing store. Reverse: raise the count at
            Recapturing, undo on refusal.
        comment     2026-11-16T10:03:03Z
